9. Technical Concepts to Be Ready to Explain
What is RUL?
Remaining Useful Life is the number of operating cycles estimated to
remain before an asset reaches its end-of-life point. In supervised
learning, the model learns to estimate RUL from labeled historical
observations.
Is this classification or regression?
It is a regression problem because the target is a numeric quantity
measured in cycles, rather than a discrete class label.
What is predictive maintenance?
Predictive maintenance uses condition data and analytical models to
estimate equipment health or future maintenance needs.
Why use sensor data over time?
A single reading may not show whether a machine is degrading. Sequences
of readings can reveal trends and changes in operating condition.
Why is FD004 challenging?
The project plan identifies multiple operating conditions and fault
modes. Sensor values can vary with operating conditions as well as
degradation, so the model must learn useful relationships without
mistaking every variation for failure progression.
Why use multiple models?
A baseline such as Linear Regression provides a simple reference. Random
Forest and boosting models can capture nonlinear relationships.
Comparing them on the same validation strategy helps determine whether
added complexity improves performance.
Why use LightGBM and XGBoost?
Both are gradient-boosted decision-tree libraries suitable for tabular
regression. They are candidates, not guaranteed winners; validation
results will determine the final model.
What is Optuna?
Optuna is a library for searching model hyperparameters, such as tree
depth, learning rate, and number of estimators. It should be used on the
training/validation setup, not to repeatedly optimize against the final
test set.
What is SHAP?
SHAP estimates feature contributions to individual predictions and can
help explain model behavior. Explanations describe model behavior, not
necessarily causal effects.
Why use Git branches?
Branches let development continue without making every intermediate
change part of the stable main branch.
What is a virtual environment?
It is an isolated Python package environment for a particular project.
What is requirements.txt?
It lists Python dependencies so another environment can install the
packages with pip install -r requirements.txt.
Why can pip check pass when an import fails?
pip check verifies declared Python package dependencies. It does not
guarantee that all native dynamic libraries required by compiled
packages are installed and discoverable by the operating system.
What does .gitignore do?
It prevents matching untracked files from being included in Git by
default. It does not automatically untrack files that were already
committed.
